{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/468141-converting-moongose-s-infernum-to-nwod","id":468141,"title":"Converting Moongose's Infernum to NWoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-03T23:28:03-07:00","id":468141,"title":"Converting Moongose's Infernum to NWoD","content":"Anyway, I just remembered, and redownloaded, this little gem of a d20 setting, wherein the players are demons. In hell, and mostly unconcerned with the world outside. That was probably a mistake, along with making the demons as well, <i>demonic </i>as possible. I'm not saying the grimdark was unwarranted, it's just that it tends to constrict character options-there's only so many pure villains it's possible to make. More importantly, though, was the complete focus on the Pit; if I'm a demon, I want to play the soul merchant with meat on the hoof, as it were.<br /> <br /> What it did right, however, was the society of the Pit and its technology. The feudal society of general backstabbers, psychically enforced promises, and sorcery is a unique and interesting one. <br /> <br /> So, I'mma going to start my own conversion of it (Mr. Paraduo has another) with some WoDifying alterations, to make them the truth behind Hunter and Inferno demons. To an extent, at least-part of the change is that the world the Hellkin live in isn't the afterlife, but an alternate Underworld, and like the other Underworld, souls move on. Eventually. They certainly stay long enough for the iliaster to flow.<br /> <br /> So, themes:<br /> <br /> <b>Theme: </b>The hellkin, for all their posturing about being above humans, ultimately possess Virtues and Vices, albeit multiple Vices. They aren't that inhuman, and one of the more human aspects to them is their need to better themselves. Thus, the ultimate theme of Hellspawn: the Infernum is one of relentless ambition; the mercenary that seeks to forge a new House, the Zethu wonderworker who blazes new fields of study for its Duke and its own elevation, the faustian sorcerer who will make the Houses acknowledge her as an equal or die trying...perhaps even that rare demon who, faced with the growth of a conscience, seeks to make something of its life not forged on the backs of the damned and the weak. The desire to be more, and what a person will burn in order to be more, is very key to understanding the society of the Pit and its incursions into the mortal world.<br /> <br /> <b>Mood: </b>Hellkin don't think they're evil, but that's mostly because they don't have much to compare it to. As a race that literally needs to conquer and corrupt to survive, demons have become a ruthless and brutal species by necessity, seeking every possible way in which they might be able to somehow gain a few more souls, a few more damned to extract the precious iliaster from. Thus, Hellspawn's mood is one of brutal survival and no small degree of cynicism, where everyone has an angle and a plan for betrayal not out of malice, but because anyone who lives in the Infernum already does. And yet, there is hope-even the most amoral hellkin can offer a Covenant out of existing loyalty or offer kindness to its Retinue because they are its friends, nothing more. The relentlessly dark nature of Hellspawn society means nothing if there are no bright spots to compare it to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T00:46:59-07:00","id":468180,"title":"","content":"They sound like a more coherent True Fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T01:03:46-07:00","id":468191,"title":"","content":"Okay, I've very little experience with homebrewing, especially for NWoD, but I own the original and GMC corebooks, all Infernum books, and I LOVE Infernum, so I would love to get in on this project, if you'll take me.<br /> <br /> Couple of suggestions, off of the bat:<br /> <br /> * Morality-analogue needs to be handled *very* carefully. Hellspawn have more in common with humans than they care to admit, but at the same time they're also very different. They're sparks of angelic essence wedded to prototype anatomies. They are born to feed on the essence of the soul itself, living weapons engineered by fallen angels. It wouldn't make sense to me if their morality meter was mostly the same as a human's. Even beyond my distaste for that in twilitfolk in general, there's also the fact that otherwise, all Hellspawn would be completely unplayable due to insanity - they need to feed off of torture and murder or die a horrible death, after all. They simply cannot be as bothered by torture, murder and soul-rending as humans are.<br /> <br /> ** Perhaps Corruption might serve as the basis for morality meter? In Infernum, Corruption is both a strength - many mutations are more potent based on your corruption, and for mortals/angels, corruption could be used to get powerups - and a weakness (makes you easier to bind).<br /> <br /> ** Alternatively, maybe the Covenant could be useful for that role? At least in terms of inspiration?<br /> <br /> * For power stat and food, I would go with the approach of &quot;demons feed upon and use Essence, but they personally call it iliaster&quot;. This meshes neatly with the existing NWoD lore - ghosts and spirits and &quot;empowered mortals&quot; all use Essence, keeps things simple, and allows for a certain homage to Infernum: it allows high Primal Urge urathra to quite neatly take the role of Infernum's benandanti.<br /> <br /> * Obvious route is to make Breed the &quot;biological axis&quot; (clan, tribe, seeming, etc) and House the &quot;social axis&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T09:24:25-07:00","id":468460,"title":"","content":"The computer ate my response, so I'll give a summarized version:<br /> <br /> Thank you!<br /> <br /> You're right about hellkin still needing to be brutal, cynical monsters-they still need to torture to live. That's key to their psychology. I was just thinking of maybe redemption not being a pipe dream-there can be other sources of iliaster, they're just never as efficient as abusing the souls.<br /> <br /> Corruption as Integrity is a great plan. Maybe something like Satiety, a la Beast-maximum helps your powers, minimum helps you slip out of Covenants easier (which also explains why demons look down on altruistic behavior-a better person is someone they can't easily control).<br /> <br /> Iliaster seems like it could be a mix to me-it's the Essence that's been refined by the Pit and transformed into something demons can digest or use to power their machines. Essence that has been harvested as Essence can only be refined into the normal boring plasmic stuff, but the big three of Strain, Sorrow, and Agony can be distilled in the human world-it's even more valuable from there, although whether that's due to any real affect or simply novelty of rarity is an open question.<br /> <br /> Obviously. I've also experimented with the idea of &quot;House Vices&quot;, which are more ideology than passion, ie they work like Virtues. Yes, this does mean a hellkin can never uphold its actual Virtue and still have full Willpower regen on occasion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T10:29:45-07:00","id":468505,"title":"","content":"Oh, I definitely agree that redemption should be possible. NWoD recognizes that it's the light within the darkness that makes the game worth playing, as Infernum does; if there's no hope to be something better, then there's little incentive to play, after all.<br /> <br /> Yes, Harmony or Satiety would be my suggested models for the Hellspawn morality equivalent. Especially if we use Corruption to take its place.<br /> <br /> Hmm... what if Iliaster is, as you suggest, &quot;refined&quot; Essence, but Hellspawn can pick up powers or devices that allow them to directly convert Essence into iliaster? I am recalling the palace augment which allows hellspawn to gain iliaster from having people worship them, as just an example. This would help with your goal of having hellspawn be redeemable; it's not something every hellspawn can do, but those who are willing to try can find other sources of nourishment that will work.<br /> <br /> A &quot;House Vice&quot; that works as a Virtue sounds like a great idea to me; really helps emphasize just how different hellspawn are to any of the other twilitfolk in the NWoD.<br /> <br /> The book's Mutations are the obvious source of powers/gifts/etc, but here's a thought dimly related: NWoD is many things, but it isn't as possible to &quot;power-boost&quot; as it is in D&amp;D. Moreover, I disliked the whole &quot;mutation tax to gain decent elemental protection&quot; thing in the D20 game. So, here's what I'd suggest: to reflect the inherent Fire Resistance of hellspawn, part of the basic template powers is that all hellspawn downgrade fire damage to Bashing. Similar elemental resistances work the same way - the first dot in the Chain of Frost downgrades cold damage to Bashing, chain of Storms downgrades electrical damage to Bashing, etc. And higher value gifts render that kind of damage completely ineffective.<br /> <br /> I'll need to pull out my reference books first, but, I could try and take a shot at drafting the Hellspawn generic template and the Breed subtemplates, just to give us somewhere to start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T14:26:34-07:00","id":468763,"title":"","content":"Actually, I can think of the Questionnaire:<br /> <br /> <b>Lies and Elements of Truth<br /> <br /> Demons are fallen angels who war on god:</b><br /> <br /> Some may be , but not us. If you believe the Morningstar (a rather stupid move) we were created by them, but hellkin are natives of hell, made from true spawn and turned intelligent. Other beings under hellspawn include the aforementioned true spawn, living humans who moved or were born in the Pit, and those double-damned Abhori. As for the God thing, honestly we don't care if there's a monotheist deity in the first place, let alone war on Him-if He gets in our way, though...<br /> <br /> <b>Demons are the evil inhabitants of an afterlife reserved for the wicked, who torture the souls of the damned.</b><br /> <br /> Not true! The Pit's only a stop on to wherever souls go when they leave! (laughs) In all seriousness, flesh, I don't think &quot;evil&quot; exists except as a cultural way to avoid how brutal this universe really is, but given our biology? I think only the truly delusional among us would seriously be offended by the e-word, if you get my meaning. And while not all the souls we get are bastards, nearly all of the ones who fall to us are, and their pain makes lots of the iliaster we need to survive, so the torture part's pretty much spot-on. If you like, I can show you some of my favored field techniques.<br /> <br /> <b>Demons are immaterial beings who possess humans to work their designs on Earth.</b><br /> <br /> Do I <i>look </i>immaterial? This canard isn't entirely false, though-hellkin can and will project their minds into humans, other hellkin, once-humans...it's kind of a headache for politics. When we're out here on Mundus, though? Most of us come as we are or weave human skins around ourselves. That isn't to say, flesh, that there aren't any immaterial demons-it's just that they happen to be nobles, and a side effect of getting a fortress in the Pit is that the noble can no longer be fleshy normally-they need a domain to &quot;rule&quot; invisibly if they don't want to get crushed under their own metaphysical weight.<br /> <br /> <b>Demons are merchants of souls who will give you anything in return for it.</b><br /> <br /> We tend to start low and work up to souls, and demons are bound by the resources we can actually pay with, but that's true. Being in the ownership of a demon is about the only gurantee that a soul will be damned after death and feeding the maws of thirsty demons and industry in the Pit. It's not so bad, though, flesh-I'm not the most vicious iliaster harvester in the world...<br /> <br /> <b>Demons are untrustworty liars who will backstab you as soon as it becomes advantageous.</b><br /> <br /> Given some of the idiots I've worked for, I wish this was more true than it actually is. See, we'll do and say anything to get ahead of the cutthroats we call fellow demons, but there's also a system of mystical pacts called Covenants-ie, debts of service and loyalty that are mystically enforced by the power of the Infernum's reality itself. It's hard to slip or even work off the Covenant without getting my brain fried, so I can't help but honor any deal I agree to. For the most part.<br /> <br /> <b>Sorcerers and demons are natural allies.</b><br /> <br /> If you're talking about faustians, true. It's easy enough for a knowledgable demon to offer sorcery in exchange for whatever, all showing some would-be demon-caller proper finger twiddling is time and tested patience. A few faustians even move to the Infernum, taking advantage of the time dilation we have to &quot;trick&quot; their bodies into not aging. Because they're often better than us at sorcery and are more resistant to Covenants, they're valued members of our society. Kind of. Lot of us resent a living human who isn't being ground underneath their heel. Not me though-I am <i>perfectly</i> fine with you knowing magic. I just expect a little, you know, working relationship afterwards.<br /> <br /> <b>Hell exists.</b><br /> <br /> You got that right. It's not anything particularly accurate to modern mythology, but it resembles it enough in passing. It's not something you're eternally bound to should you die and get damned, and I hear it's possible for some particularly ambitious souls to become hellkin (don't quote me on that), but it's certainly a place where souls go if they've fucked up in life and do not have a fun time of it. They can't-we need their suffering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T16:01:54-07:00","id":468915,"title":"","content":"Nice. Couple of random thoughts from me:<br /> <br /> * Since hellspawn are native to their own plane of existence, I'd suggest that rather than forcing them to take human form, it's an option - the Chain of Man mutation exists in D20 for a reason, after all. You can choose to play either an Infernum-only campaign, a Mundus-only campaign (in which case they get the &quot;Chain of Man&quot; for free), or both.<br /> <br /> * Basic template notes; Corruption as morals meter, &quot;Reserves&quot; as Power Stat, Iliaster as Power Fuel, take only Bashing damage from Fire.<br /> <br /> * Covenanting perhaps based on VTR2e's Viniculum?<br /> <br /> * Before tackling sub-templates (Breeds), we should establish whether we want to try and accurately convert their D20 abilities or their motif. Also, closer to Blood &amp; Smoke, or to DTD in terms of how they impact upon the base template?<br /> <br /> * Faustian: perhaps a &quot;minor template&quot; analogous to Ghouls or 2e Wolfbloods might be the best way to handle them? They are, after all, basically humans who have learned to practice hellish ritual magic in D20.<br /> <br /> Hmm... I think I can do a Breed Stereotypes litany, if you'd like me to try my hand at that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T16:42:39-07:00","id":468946,"title":"","content":"Probably good points, all of them. And faustians seem like a more-powerful-than-average minor template, if only because they have access to something pretty powerful.<br /> <br /> And I'd like that writeup, thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T17:47:42-07:00","id":469013,"title":"","content":"Alright, this is a pretty rough-scrabble interpretation, but I hope maybe it's a talking point?<br /> <br /> Artificer<br /> * Beast: We do the work and they take the credit. Still, sometimes it's worth it; they NEED us, and the ideas they have...<br /> * Deceiver: Arrogant bastards. All those fancy schemes of theirs would be nothing without us work.<br /> * Fiend: Too in love with the skies to think about doing a real cycle's work.<br /> * Hulk: Big and DUMB. Just give them the armor and weapons they want and they'll stay out of the way.<br /> * Imp: Annoying little chatterboxes, that's one thing. When they mess around with your projects, that's another.<br /> * Malcubus: Lazy sluts; we work out guts out for the Lords and they just have to stand around looking pretty.<br /> * Slaver: Too eager with those whips by half. In their eyes, we're little different than the damned.<br /> * Stalker: Little more than trained animals. Always off chasing something. So long as it keeps them out of the workshop, I suppose.<br /> <br /> Beast<br /> * Artificer: The perfect little partners. We're the brains, they're the hands. Still, sometimes hands stray...<br /> * Deceiver: Too impressed with themselves by far.<br /> * Fiend: Dangerous, to be sure, but not as dangerous as they think.<br /> * Hulk: Mindless brutes... but, yes, useful for the heavy lifting.<br /> * Imp: Cleverness avails nothing without courage.<br /> * Malcubus: They trust far too much in the power of flesh.<br /> * Slaver: Simple-minded thugs, but necessary.<br /> * Stalker: The difference between them and us? Our minds have risen beyond our feral origins. Theirs haven't.<br /> <br /> Deceiver<br /> * Artificer: The most fundamental of tools for our needs. But don't let them get ideas above their stations.<br /> * Beast: Tread carefully around them. You never know if they'll come for you with snapping jaws or a curse from afar. Use them with care.<br /> * Fiend: Their pride is their weakness. Use it.<br /> * Hulk: Too mindless to train, too vicious to trust, too useful to ignore.<br /> * Imp: Mewling little runts... but, they can be so useful at ferretting out secrets for you. Offer them strength, and use them to your advantage.<br /> * Malcubus: Take your pleasure from them, it's what they were made for, but never let them know what you're thinking.<br /> * Slaver: Oafish thugs, but there is a certain something to admire in someone who knows their place and enjoys it.<br /> * Stalker: Hounds that walk. Treat them as such.<br /> <br /> Fiend<br /> * Artificer: Better to be dead than to be like them, trapped on the ground and crawling like vermin.<br /> * Beast: Perhaps a distant relative, but still, they will never know the power of the skies.<br /> * Deceiver: They think themselves leaders. Weaklings.<br /> * Hulk: Far beneath us. We are the true warriors of Hell.<br /> * Imp: A blight upon the skies, vermin not fit to share the air with us.<br /> * Malcubus: Trophies fit to grace our arms and little more.<br /> * Slaver: Someone has to keep the larders stocked. Better them than us.<br /> * Stalker: They think themselves our kin. As if ground-crawlers can ever understand the true meaning of hunting.<br /> <br /> Hulk<br /> * Artificer: Little runts. Don't squish 'em if they can give you stuff for fighting with.<br /> * Beast: Rely too much on spooky stuff wen they could be rippin' an' tearin'.<br /> * Deceiver: Yeah, boss, we'll go stomp that. Cowards.<br /> * Fiend: Decent scrappers, but damn arrogant. You won't be so cocky when I rip them wings off yer.<br /> * Imp: Won't never challenge ya, but don't listen to 'em all the time. Make sure to squish a few now an' then, so they don't think yer just a tool.<br /> * Malcubus: Pretty...<br /> * Slaver: Hey? You wanna pick a fight with me? ...Didn't think so, loser.<br /> * Stalker: They can lead ya to a fight, but they won't stick around for it.<br /> <br /> Imp<br /> * Artificer: Worse off even than us. Too haughty to see how to wriggle out of their chains.<br /> * Beast: Dangerous. Clever, too clever by far. But they know we can be useful.<br /> * Deceiver: Our 'illustrious' masters. Tell them what they want to know and they won't use you.<br /> * Fiend: The worst combination of traits; arrogant, hotheaded AND vicious. Avoid them if you can, make yourself useful and not worth hurting if you can't.<br /> * Hulk: It's not fair! So much power, all under the control of so small a brain! If you can tame one, it's so worth it... but they get mad so easily, too...<br /> * Malcubus: They know a lot more than other hellspawn give them credit for. Don't underestimate them.<br /> * Slaver: Don't get too close. They'll have you for lunch as readily as a damned.<br /> * Stalker: Stay away; they like to chase anything smaller than them.<br /> <br /> Malcubus<br /> * Artificer: Poor, proud thing. Why don't you take a break? There's more to life than just work...<br /> * Beast: And they say we're perverse...<br /> * Deceiver: Tell them that they're clever and pretty, and they'll be all to eager to tell you why they are.<br /> * Fiend: Too proud to realise their own folly.<br /> * Hulk: Very useful toys, they just need a little delicacy to tame.<br /> * Imp: They can tell you such interesting things if you ask them right.<br /> * Slaver: I suppose pleasure is pleasure. They certainly can be generous patrons if you please them right.<br /> * Stalker: Too lean and hungry to tempt conventionally. Still malleable, if you know the right methods.<br /> <br /> Slaver<br /> * Artificer: Work, scum! You have your place, so you'll do what you're told!<br /> * Beast: Greedy bastards; do you know how much iliaster you waste on your crazy schemes?<br /> * Deceiver: Leave the thinking to them - that way, they get the blame when it all goes wrong.<br /> * Fiend: All high and mighty... until they need a feed, of course.<br /> * Hulk: Use your lash wisely, or they'll tear you apart. They're higher on the foodchain than you, and don't forget it.<br /> * Imp: Cringing little wretches. Still, it's worth listening to them; they make wonderful informants.<br /> * Malcubus: Pleasure. Pain. Let me show you some sides to them you've never dreamed of...<br /> * Stalker: You track 'em, we torment 'em. Good partners.<br /> <br /> Stalker<br /> * Artificer: Stumpy little think-meats. Useless for hunting.<br /> * Beast: Alpha horrors. Better to run with them than to run before them.<br /> * Deceiver: They point, we go.<br /> * Fiend: Great hunters. Maybe greater than us. But assume too much.<br /> * Hulk: They are like gorgoths. Big and dumb, but dangerous. Worthy prey, worthy pack.<br /> * Imp: Little scavengers. Still, they can lead us to the prey.<br /> * Malcubus: What can they offer, compared to the hunt?<br /> * Slaver: We feed them, they feed us. Good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T22:43:53-07:00","id":469180,"title":"","content":"Nice. I'll try to get around to being more thorough later, but nice start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T23:40:55-07:00","id":469224,"title":"","content":"Glad you like. Here, I'll be more helpful and throw in the other races (minus Beasts, since we don't really know anything about them yet.<br /> <br /> Also, something to consider; I don't know, maybe Disquiet is getting reworked for twilitfolk in general in 2e, but given hellspawn themselves are raw soul-stuff shackled in a body of protoflesh, I'd say that's a pretty decent grounds to consider them immune to Disquiet.<br /> <br /> Artificer<br /> Mortals - You think your creations are impressive? I'll show you true genius.<br /> <br /> Vampires - Machines that run on blood aren't new to me. Never seen something like you before.<br /> <br /> Werewolves - Howling beasts! Your savagery is nothing to my technology!<br /> <br /> Mages - I'm almost impressed. If you could make it work when you need it.<br /> <br /> Prometheans - What are you? Can I make more like you?<br /> <br /> Changelings - Plenty of cold iron in my workshop, faerie. You don't scare me.<br /> <br /> Hunters - Nice gun. Mine's bigger.<br /> <br /> Sin-eaters - The dead are fuel for my furnaces, oil for my engines, grist for my mills. I'll add you to them next.<br /> <br /> Mummies - A relic like you belongs in the past, with all the other ancient, useless junk.<br /> <br /> <br /> Beast<br /> Mortals - Insignificant vermin. You are food for my belly and fuel for my magic. Nothing more.<br /> <br /> Vampires - Defying death, working magic through the medium of blood and corpse-meat. Fascinating.<br /> <br /> Werewolves - Raw magic hidden beneath a veneer of such savagery. I wonder just how different we really are beneath the skin...<br /> <br /> Mages - You show such promise, such interesting things... yes, I think there is much we could learn from each other...<br /> <br /> Prometheans - Why would you want to be human? You are so much better now!<br /> <br /> Changelings - This Arcadia sounds intriguing. Come, little faerie, share with me; I can promise you my protection if you will.<br /> <br /> Hunters - You're cleverer than the rest of the vermin, I'll give you that. But you underestimate me, and so you shall feed me.<br /> <br /> Sin-eaters - Such strange powers... fascinating. Come to me; let me tease the secrets of the soul from your fusion... what things you will teach me...<br /> <br /> Mummies - Come now, surely you must remember something? Damn your eyes, you WILL teach me what you know!<br /> <br /> <br /> Deceiver<br /> Mortals - I'm sorry, did you really think you were getting the better end of the deal?<br /> <br /> Vampires - Even I cannot cheat death the way you can. I applaud your skills. Shall we do business?<br /> <br /> Werewolves - If you're looking to hunt information, that can be arranged. For a price.<br /> <br /> Mages - You know you want to make the deal. Of course this is legitimate; don't you trust me?<br /> <br /> Prometheans - You want a soul? I can arrange that. What? Install it into you? That'll be extra.<br /> <br /> Changelings - Tell me more about these 'Goblin Markets', and I may give you a discount.<br /> <br /> Hunters - Come now, can't we make a deal? No? A pity... for you.<br /> <br /> Sin-eaters - Everything has a price, my friend.<br /> <br /> Mummies - Now, now, friend; you scratch my back and I'll scratch yours.<br /> <br /> <br /> Fiend<br /> Mortals - I shall make torches of you all!<br /> <br /> Vampires - Worms walking about in shell of dead meat. You burn so easily.<br /> <br /> Werewolves - What is your savagery when you cannot meet me in the skies?<br /> <br /> Mages - Your power is admirable, but it pales compared to mine.<br /> <br /> Prometheans - Cease your prattle, I have no time for your moaning.<br /> <br /> Changelings - Cower back in your holes, wretch. I will burn my enemies where they stand.<br /> <br /> Hunters - You think to hunt me, ground-crawlers?!<br /> <br /> Sin-eaters - The dead are dead, and let them stay dead.<br /> <br /> Mummies - Your treasure shall be mine, and you shall BURN!<br /> <br /> <br /> Hulk<br /> Mortals - Squish food. Eat food.<br /> <br /> Vampires - Taste bad. Not worth it.<br /> <br /> Werewolves - You mad. Me madder!<br /> <br /> Mages - Squish 'em fore they makes the nasty lights.<br /> <br /> Prometheans - You tough one... you die hard, die well.<br /> <br /> Changelings - Run away, hide, and me leave you 'lone.<br /> <br /> Hunters - Me will smash your face!<br /> <br /> Sin-eaters - Why you got two souls? Double-yummies for me!<br /> <br /> Mummies - Me no want eat you. Smell bad.<br /> <br /> <br /> Imp<br /> Mortals - So gullible, so foolish. But dangerous, if cornered.<br /> <br /> Vampires - These bastards scare me. They're always working some angle, and they keep eyeing me up like a tasty treat.<br /> <br /> Werewolves - Scary! Stay away or die screaming. Those are your only choices.<br /> <br /> Mages - So much power... find one you can flatter and glue your lips to their ass. You won't regret it.<br /> <br /> Prometheans - Kind of gullible, and strong enough to be worth it, but don't stick around if they figure you're messing with them. You'll go squish otherwise.<br /> <br /> Changelings - ...I think they're even more scared than we are. See if you can use that.<br /> <br /> Hunters - Avoid them if you can. Trick them or trap them if you can't.<br /> <br /> Sin-eaters - Only thing worse than an uppity soul is one walking around in a protective meat-suit with all kinds of nasty magic. Stay away.<br /> <br /> Mummies - DON'T get involved. You have nothing they want.<br /> <br /> <br /> Malcubus<br /> Mortals - Come on, baby, you know you want to touch me...<br /> <br /> Vampires - Feral, passionate, seductive, deadly... we have so much in common.<br /> <br /> Werewolves - Down, girl. I like it rough, but you're a bit too much.<br /> <br /> Mages - Mmm, I could really fall for someone like you.<br /> <br /> Prometheans - Trapped on the outside, unable to enjoy even the simplest of pleasures? That's a hell beyond anything I can imagine.<br /> <br /> Changelings - Come now, surely you learned something of pain and pleasure in your Durance? I want to know...<br /> <br /> Hunters - How dare you raise your hands to me! I will swallow your soul for this!<br /> <br /> Sin-eaters - Two for one, huh? I've done kinkier things.<br /> <br /> Mummies - No, I wasn't eying your dusty old relics. I have better taste than that.<br /> <br /> <br /> Slaver<br /> Mortals - Come here, it's time for you to get shelled.<br /> <br /> Vampires - Expired goods. Useless.<br /> <br /> Werewolves - Savage and primal. Strong enough to endure many torments.<br /> <br /> Mages - The purity of your soul... I will FEAST!<br /> <br /> Prometheans - I can bend any slave to their proper place. That includes you, corpse-thing.<br /> <br /> Changelings - Hmm... tis a flickering thing, but exoticness can be valuable.<br /> <br /> Hunters - Meat should not try to bite back.<br /> <br /> Sin-eaters - A two-for-one special; you'll make delicious iliaster indeed.<br /> <br /> Mummies - You're way past your expiry date.<br /> <br /> <br /> Stalker<br /> Mortals - Run.<br /> <br /> Vampires - You think yourself predators? Hah.<br /> <br /> Werewolves - Let's see who is the better hunter.<br /> <br /> Mages - The greatest quarry.<br /> <br /> Prometheans - You are not worth hunting.<br /> <br /> Changelings - You will never outrun me, no matter who you outran before.<br /> <br /> Hunters - Prey that tries to fight is still prey.<br /> <br /> Sin-eaters - Greater risk, greater reward.<br /> <br /> Mummies - Dead and buried, just not accepting it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T18:23:49-07:00","id":469715,"title":"","content":"Also nice. My first instinct is that I would have put the <i>other </i>demons in there, but (A) that's massively confusing and probably a bit of bloat to have both demon PCs existing in the same setting, and (B) it's actually fitting if the Infernum at large doesn't know about the Unchained or their former master; it keeps the Church of the Morningstar's truths behind a &quot;scam&quot; religion part of the setting, and also points out that the hellkin are actually pretty distant from the world, since the Machine is entirely an Earthly phenomenon. And I kind of suspect Unchained in the know want to keep it that way, given how fallen angels are incidental support of the Luciferian Heresy-and thus a likely target of a pogrom to keep the Houses' apparent legitimacy of rule in the Pit intact. Can't let the Free Cities have an inch, now, can we?<br /> <br /> EDIT: And now that I think about it, Infernum and Descent's themes don't really mix. In Infernum, you're a potential prince trying to claw your way to the top of a power structure, build a new one, or at least make yourself indispensable to it. In Descent, you're a fugitive from a power structure that will always hate you for disobeying it, and any power you gain is mostly for the sake of safety from your loyal brethren. Kind of hard to mix the two, especially given how unsafe the Pit is by nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 04-05-2015, 09:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T19:08:20-07:00","id":469745,"title":"","content":"Well, in fairness, the GMC and DTD corebooks both mention that the GodMachine does extend its reach into parallel realities and alternate timelines and the like. That said, given the nature of time in the Pit causes issues with electronics, it could indeed be a &quot;dead zone&quot; even to the GodMachine.<br /> <br /> To be honest, I'm not too happy with my efforts here, personally. I think they kind of miss the feel of the hellspawn breeds in many ways - the fiend's arrogant pride as the fiery flying knights of Hell, the beast's hunger for flesh and sorcerer, the slaver's eager cruelty. But hopefully they can be reworked to be something better.<br /> <br /> Something that perhaps should be touched upon as part of this project is this: the fact that Hellspawn have something no other twilitfolk has. And that is a Place Of Their Own. All of the other twilits are parasites, hiding in the occult underground of human society - Hellspawn have an entire world to call their own. They don't fear humanity the way the others do, because humans aren't such a threat - they can always retreat to their world, and any human who follows is &quot;certain&quot; to die horribly in a world that isn't their own. Even a full-scale war between Hellspawn and humanity isn't so terrifying a concept, because, for a lot of reasons, hellspawn could conceivably WIN such a conflict.<br /> <br /> Yes, I can elaborate on that if you want.<br /> <br /> Hmm... if we want to go the whole hog here, we could actually include &quot;hellbred&quot; (half-demon) as a minor supernatural template alongside the Faustians. Additionally, or alternatively, we could include &quot;Mutants&quot;, the ability for mortals to take Hellish Mutations as supernatural merits - this would reflect how mortals could pick up Corruption and thus Mutation in the D20 version.<br /> <br /> On those lines, I could honestly see a &quot;Pit Gazetteer&quot; including the Sons of Bor (Cancer Compact [ala Promethean Brotherhood or the Hunt Club] filled with Faustians and Mutants and Hellbred) and the Knights of the Harrowing as Infernum Hunter material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T21:57:30-07:00","id":469866,"title":"","content":"That's actually a good point.<br /> <br /> I'd also try to balance it against the fact that humans are supposed to be dangerous as masses in the nWoD. Hm, maybe we could have it that the fate-warping effect the living have on the Pit also has that effect on hellgouts and other places which have been corrupted by Hell. Which means a fullscale war is also one that would likely end up being a very fair one, as the amount of corruption produced would end up giving humanity at large the ability to sway fate everywhere to their advantage-and given how backstabby demons are, humans would definitely be more united.<br /> <br /> Of course, there's also the mechanics of the Infernum, which make it hard to really conquer anything outside of it-it's not easy, crossing that barrier regularly.<br /> <br /> I should also be pulling my own weight again, I'll start working on an intro-while juggling my other goal, writing that fanfic's first chapter, so that may take a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T22:24:20-07:00","id":469880,"title":"","content":"Humans are dangerous as masses, in the NWoD, by virtue of the fact that humans outnumber twilitfolk at a ratio of about 1000 to 1. Hellspawn number in the billions, equivalent to humanity easily. They also breed much more effectively than humans - it takes 1 demon to make up to 18 new ones, if you look at the Spawning Pit description in Book 3 - to the point that the biggest role of the Circle of Slaughter in the modern era is keeping the population of hellspawn *down* to manageable levels.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, it takes the better part of 2 decades to take a human from &quot;conception&quot; to &quot;trained soldier ready to kill&quot;. For hellspawn, it takes eighteen *months*. So not only is a hellspawn army easily as big as a human one? They can reinforce themselves much more effectively. When a human soldier's supply lines are cut and he runs out of ammo, he's pretty much screwed. A hellspawn is a living weapon. From the moment it claws its way out of the pupation chrysalis, a hellspawn is ready to kill. No training, nor education, nor armament needed.<br /> <br /> So it's a good thing for both sides that war isn't likely to happen. A hellspawn invasion would be a nightmare for humanity, and as useful as fatebending can be, let's not forget that the modern army depends a lot on fancy electronics to do its job - gear that's utterly useless in the Pit.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm not saying that war between earth and hell should be looked into. Just that hellspawn have a place where *they* belong, and that should be taken into account.<br /> <br /> A human in Infernum has to explore the horror of having gone from the top of the foodchain to the bottom. Even a hunter in the NWoD can take a grim hope in the knowledge that others will take up the Vigil. In the Pit? You are the one who must hide and fear the wrath of the slumbering giant if it wakes.<br /> <br /> Of course, in the mortal world, a hellspawn is just as out of their element. Overconfidence, and the perils it can bring, are some of the themes that a hellspawn amongst mortals can explore.<br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking of hellgouting, here's something I was considering: rework it so that it justifies hellspawn having a &quot;return home&quot; intrinistic power whilst they manifest in the mundus. They can slip home freely (though getting back to the mundus is another story), but it's a skill challenge to try and take other beings or even locations back with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T06:24:57-07:00","id":470088,"title":"","content":"Good point, and good plan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T11:42:11-07:00","id":470292,"title":"","content":"Hmm... I can't do the crunch, sadly, I'm not that good at the NWoD 2e mechanics, but if you wanted, I could take a shot at the Breed writeups following the conventions set out in Demon The Descent or Vampire 2e/Blood &amp; Smoke.<br /> <br /> Only thing is, before I can do that, I need to know if we should try and set a more specific appearance to the breeds, or leave them looking vague beyond their designated traits, as in the D20 version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T14:12:16-07:00","id":470348,"title":"","content":"Well, neither am I, but I was always intending to try. I think I can think of thematic mechanics.<br /> <br /> The less specific appearance is probably something that should be kept, though. The sheer <i>variety </i>of the hellkin is a big point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T15:07:58-07:00","id":470403,"title":"","content":"Well, the Blood &amp; Smoke and DTD &quot;race outlines&quot; aren't as intuitive as I thought, so forgive me for my mistakes here. I'll start with one Breed and see for feedback first before I move on to the next.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm guessing we're going with the idea of the Houses and other Factions as the &quot;social splat&quot;?<br /> <br /> <br /> Artificers<br /> The Devils in the Machine<br /> <br /> Any society that wishes to function must have those who make things, and Hell is no exception. Though damned souls toil in countless numbers to provide the brute labor - or raw materials - upon which the Infernum is supported, it is the artificers who truly create the Infernum. They are the engineers and the architects, toiling ceaselessly to shape metal, stone, flesh, bone, soulstuff and other, more esoteric materials upon which hellish civilisation depends for buildings, tools, weapons, everything.<br /> <br /> And yet, hell has little gratitude to spare. Artificers have long been commodities at best, dismissed as little different to the tools they wield at worst. Even though the black economy of torment and destruction rests upon their squared shoulders, other, &quot;nobler&quot; hellspawn have looked past them. Small wonder, then, that the artificers have been involved with and supportive of the Free City Heresy since the beginning. Some wonder in private if maybe the artificers somehow created the Heresy.<br /> <br /> Appearance: Artificers are as variable as all hellspawn, but there are certain traits that define them. All artificers are smaller than humans, averaging a childish stature. They are rarely as scrawny as imps, though they vary from squat, muscular dwarfs to eerie fey child-things whose delicate limbs, so perfectly suited for worming into machines to work upon them from inside, conceal a hellish strength. Supple, many-fingered hands are definitive to these hellspawn; they frequently have more fingers than a human should, and they are common longer and/or more heavily jointed than a human's. Some may have tentacles, mechanical plugs or similar accouterments in lieu of fingers. Tied to the machines by their nature, metal and machinery is a frequent component of their physical frames, often increasingly overtaking their flesh as they grow in power. This may vary from plating of metal upon their skin to visibly mechanical limbs and organs intermeshed with their bodies to machinery of metal and/or bone tearing its way through their bodies.<br /> <br /> Visiting Mundus: Artificers have less interest in the mortal world compared to some hellspawn, but they still find reasons to visit. Some are summoned to work for ambitious sorcerers, or by small cults hoping for infernal revelations into the sciences or possibilities of occult engineering; this latter group is likely to find an appreciative audience, for it is rare that artificers have willing students. Other artificers sneak through into the mortal world to find inspiration, or retrieve rare ingredients for their projects, or simply to hide from the cruel masters in the Infernum.<br /> <br /> <br /> ...Not sure what else to really write. Especially to avoid simply copy-pasting the D20 stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T19:28:58-07:00","id":473666,"title":"","content":"Take a page from Blood &amp; Smoke, methinks. A big way to make the writeups a little different is to show each breed at work in various different roles. Three to a breed should work.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T21:20:32-07:00","id":473827,"title":"","content":"Hmm... maybe. Y'know what? How about you post a template for the Breed and/or House writeups and I'll see about filling 'em up for you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T22:49:14-07:00","id":473905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/468141-converting-moongose-s-infernum-to-nwod?p=473827#post473827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... maybe. Y'know what? How about you post a template for the Breed and/or House writeups and I'll see about filling 'em up for you?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Okay, basic, basic stuff before I go to bed:<br /> <br /> [Breed Name]<br /> <br /> [Thematic Descriptor-a one sentence-at-the-most of how they interact with the Infernum and Mundus; Artificers would be the Keepers of Mechanisms, Malcubi would be Merchants of Vice, Hulks Destroyers, etc.]<br /> <br /> [Longer description, including role in Infernum]<br /> <br /> [Role on Earth and why they'd go to Mundus]<br /> <br /> [Three-to-four types of general character, different enough from each other to seem varied-one should always be a seeming oddball, like an imp warrior who sneaks across the battlefield to find weak points, or a slaver &quot;good cop&quot; who specializes in both caring for the damned so they don't break permanently and psychological torment).<br /> <br /> [Three sections: Why we're the best breed, why humans need us, how we fall from out heights]<br /> <br /> [Specialized Condition-thinking Werewolf 2e cribbing here, a self-inflicted buff to a specialized task that leads to a weakness later on]<br /> <br /> [Characters: Their general personality and attribute/skill spread, along what theme their Virtues and Vices organize themselves along.]<br /> <br /> [Breed Mutation]<br /> <br /> [Weakness]<br /> <br /> [Stereotypes of other breeds]<br /> <br /> [Examples of House and Free City characters]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T04:00:11-07:00","id":474054,"title":"","content":"Okay, thanks, I can't guarantee I can fill all of them details, especially the more crunchy parts, but I should be able to give you a skeleton to frame up.<br /> <br /> <br /> Artificer<br /> Keepers of the Infernal Engines<br /> <br /> In The Infernum:<br /> Any society that wishes to function must have those who make things, and Hell is no exception. Though damned souls toil in countless numbers to provide the brute labor - or raw materials - upon which the Infernum is supported, it is the artificers who truly create the Infernum. They are the engineers and the architects, toiling ceaselessly to shape metal, stone, flesh, bone, soulstuff and other, more esoteric materials upon which hellish civilisation depends for buildings, tools, weapons, everything.<br /> <br /> And yet, hell has little gratitude to spare. Artificers have long been commodities at best, dismissed as little different to the tools they wield at worst. Even though the black economy of torment and destruction rests upon their squared shoulders, other, &quot;nobler&quot; hellspawn have looked past them. Small wonder, then, that the artificers have been involved with and supportive of the Free City Heresy since the beginning. Some wonder in private if maybe the artificers somehow created the Heresy.<br /> <br /> Artificers are as variable as all hellspawn when it comes to appearance, but there are certain traits that define them. All artificers are smaller than humans, averaging a childish stature. They are rarely as scrawny as imps, though they vary from squat, muscular dwarfs to eerie fey child-things whose delicate limbs, so perfectly suited for worming into machines to work upon them from inside, conceal a hellish strength. Supple, many-fingered hands are definitive to these hellspawn; they frequently have more fingers than a human should, and they are common longer and/or more heavily jointed than a human's. Some may have tentacles, mechanical plugs or similar accouterments in lieu of fingers. Tied to the machines by their nature, metal and machinery is a frequent component of their physical frames, often increasingly overtaking their flesh as they grow in power. This may vary from plating of metal upon their skin to visibly mechanical limbs and organs intermeshed with their bodies to machinery of metal and/or bone tearing its way through their bodies.<br /> <br /> <br /> Upon the Mundus:<br /> Within the Mundus, artificers serve much the same role as they do in the Infernum. They are engineers, architects, medics, beast-handlers, and other roles where their keen grasp of the sciences of machinery and flesh may be useful. Although artificers have been known to slip through into the Mundus of their own free will, generally for the sake of hiding, gathering rarer materials or particular prime souls, or to seek inspiration for new infernal engines, it is much more common that they are summoned by exterior forces.<br /> <br /> Hellspawn prefer to summon artificers for matters relating to mortal sciences and technology - the typical artificer in the Mundus serves as a brood's &quot;techno-wizard&quot; or &quot;smart guy&quot;, using its hellish insight into all forms of machinery and sciences to aid them in whatever schemes have brought the brood to the Mundus in the first place. <br /> <br /> Mortal summoners are less common in the modern era than they once were, but still possible. Scientists driven to the brink of madness by their obsession with some technological marvel - or horror - may summon one or more artificers to their side to create it, or to teach them how to make it themselves. Maybe even doing so as a result of whispers sent to them across the void by the artificers in the first place. Other hell-cults with delusions of grandeur may summon artificers to create elaborate manors to dwell in, or diabolical traps to protect what is theirs.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sample Characters:<br /> #1: Your &quot;bog standard&quot; artificer, this hellspawn focuses on Mental skills, predominantly those related to engineering and electronics. He hacks, he cobbles bombs, he builds things, he maintains ally gear, and generally is intended to stay off of the front-lines and back behind doing tech support.<br /> <br /> #2: This warrior artificer uses his small stature and intelligence to be an expert trapsmith, assassin, spy, saboteur and marksman. Much as he prefers to crawl in through vents and rig the building to detonate, or snipe from afar, sneaking up on someone and murdering them isn't beyond his skill range either.<br /> <br /> #3: This artificer defies the stereotype and approaches social interactions as just another complicated mechanism to pick apart and rebuild. Placing Social first and Mental second, he excels at dissecting the minds of others (metaphorically speaking) and then using that knowledge to his advantage.<br /> <br /> <br /> Building Artificer Characters:<br /> The typical Artificer puts Mental skills first, Physical skills second and Social skills last. The mind is most important, but the strength to carry heavy loads of raw parts, devices or big guns is also valuable. Social skills suffer, at least if you're playing to stereotypes. The most common Virtues relate to endurance or technical skill - the artificer who takes pride in his diligence, his control, his intellect. Fortitude and Prudence are the most iconic Virtues. The most common Vices relate to their egos and need for respect, though their repressed resentment also finds common expression - Pride, Envy and Wrath, in other words.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T06:16:10-07:00","id":474214,"title":"","content":"I imagine faustians sorcerers still need to torture people in order to gather Illiaster to fuel their magick, right","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T07:38:18-07:00","id":474291,"title":"","content":"Excellent! I'll start thinking of the crunch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T14:14:39-07:00","id":474892,"title":"","content":"Cool. Should I start doing this for the Beast next, or wait until we're both happy with the completed Artificer before that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T18:56:22-07:00","id":475205,"title":"","content":"...Actually, completing the Artificer probably requires mechanics, as well as ways the Condition I spoke of interacts with the rest of the system.<br /> <br /> I think working on Beasts next is good.<br /> <br /> (Maybe something similar to 2E Renown is good for Chains, keeps the XP tax lower).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T23:03:59-07:00","id":476710,"title":"","content":"Alright then, I'll see what I can do. Here's a shot at the Beast for you; I just wish I could be more helpful.<br /> <br /> Beast<br /> Magi of Blood<br /> <br /> In The Infernum:<br /> Laying claim as one of the oldest and most important of the breeds, the feral forms of these hellspawn belies their keen intelligence and perverse ingenuity. They are the scholars and sages, scientist-wizards from whom most of the innovations and technologies of the Pit have flown. Artificer hands may labor to give life to their vision, but it was this breed who designed the first torture palaces, who pioneered the arts of sorcerery, who mastered the art of soul-binding and luring mortals into Hell's embrace.<br /> <br /> Beasts can be found throughout the Pit, in every conceivable role. Hermit scholars of sin and sorcerery who dedicate eternity to abstruse occultic projects, mercenary warrior-wizards, advisors in the fields of leadership, generals, sorcerers, and petty kings amongst the damned. Beasts gravitate towards positions of authority, propelled by their intellect and focus, and driven by their feral hungers.<br /> <br /> Hellspawn show great variety in their forms, but even they find beasts to be twisted and hideous creatures. Growing ever more feral as they age, the least terrifying of beasts resemble a perverse melding of man and beast. Many others resemble nothing human except maybe in vaguest outlines - nightmarish chimeras born from the imaginings of the most demented souls.<br /> <br /> <br /> Upon The Mundus:<br /> Beasts are second in entering the Mundus of their own free will only to deceivers, and second in being summoned only to malcubi.<br /> <br /> Beasts need souls perhaps more than any other breed, to sate their hunger for the raw fuel to conduct their blasphemous experimentation. Their perverse interests in living humans - as test subjects for some, as food for others, and as playmates for the most perverse - only enhances this desire. So it is that many beasts turn their sorcerous abilities towards breaching the veil and finding their way to the world of man. There, they found cults and seduce minions, offering their skills as teachers in the black arts - or even as untraceable killers - to lure the unwitting into embracing corruption, and damning themselves to be fodder in Hell.<br /> <br /> Yet other beasts are summoned by hell-cultists and would-be sorcerers, and often the beast is not unwilling in its participation. Most commonly they are summoned to be teachers - their effectiveness at tutelage in the black arts or in an advisory role having leaked to the mortal world in certain corrupt texts. Others, more foolish, seek to employ the beasts as living weapons, agents of their own will. These latter cults are most likely to be subverted, either destroyed for their affrontery or twisted to the beast's will, as they foolishly underestimate the true malign cunning that lies behind the inhuman facade. In truth, it is rare indeed where a would-be master does not ultimately find itself conquered and made the slave of the beast.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sample Characters:<br /> #1: This beast is a hermit, with little need for even the fripperies of infernal civilisation. Dedicated to the mastery of sorcerery, it focuses on enhancing its mind and, secondarily, its body. Social niceties are a weakness that it refuses to allow to poison its skill. Although abrasive and unpleasant in the extreme, with little tolerance for those who cannot keep up with its mind, its sheer power as a sorcerer allows it to command a high price.<br /> <br /> #2: This beast has pursued a particularly unlikely course for one of its breed; the path of the healer. Fascinated by the way that flesh, bone and ichor move and can be made to move, it has delved deeper and deeper into the arts of manipulating - and, ultimately, preserving - life. Its ministrations may rarely be pleasant, and are certain to leave scars of some kind, but in its own way, it is a devout medic, mending injuries with a macabre mirth as it hones its skill.<br /> <br /> #3: Whereas most beasts are predators of flesh and blood, this beast is one for minds and souls. Social, charismatic and affable, it interacts with others with surprising adroitness. Beneath its affable exterior lies a hungry for more; those who think it a friend are likely to find themselves its prey once it has satisfied its need to bind them to its will.<br /> <br /> <br /> Building Beast Characters:<br /> Mental Skills are almost always Primary for beasts, though whether Physical or Social is secondary is more individualistic. Iconically, they focus on Mutations and Sorcery over other forms of merit, save those relating to their twisted physiques or their ownership of cultists, slaves or indentured allies. They tend to specialise their skills in branches relating to either the occult or to more abstract areas - a beast is more likely to know how to hack computers than how to forge metal, for example. Diligence, Temperance and similar demonstrations of control, dedication or superiority are the most common Virtues, whilst Wrath and Pride are the most common Vices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T07:41:26-07:00","id":476938,"title":"","content":"Looks nice. Can't really say anything else right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T17:17:52-07:00","id":479620,"title":"","content":"Kind of distracted in real life... what do you think of these Titles for the remaining breeds?<br /> <br /> Deceivers: Silver-Tongued Liesmiths<br /> <br /> Fiends: Knights of the Burning Skies<br /> <br /> Hulks: Instruments of Destruction<br /> <br /> Imps: Worms of the Mind<br /> <br /> Malcubi: Merchants of Vice<br /> <br /> Slavers: Purveyors of Torment<br /> <br /> Stalkers: Hounds of Hell","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T17:32:19-07:00","id":479671,"title":"","content":"Hulks should probably be the Arms of Destruction, given the pun, but they look grand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T07:19:01-07:00","id":480199,"title":"","content":"While the idea of the infernum devils and the unchained coexisting doesn't bother me, what are the plans for infernum with the rules from Inferno?<br /> <br /> Can the demons possess mortals to make the possessed? Are you going to allow the infernum demons to make pacts like in inferno? I'm rereading the books now, but I don't remember anything much like the pact system.<br /> <br /> What are the thoughts on supernaturals getting sucked into hell, or a denizen or even native human gaining a template? Does the artificial sun of Hell burn vampires?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 04-14-2015, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T07:28:02-07:00","id":480222,"title":"","content":"Infernum didn\u00b4t have, sadly, rules for pacting with mortals or granting boons for souls. It was also implied demons, in recent times, didn\u00b4t deal directly with the mortal realm as much as before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T07:39:45-07:00","id":480224,"title":"","content":"Since you guys haven't decided on any hard mechanics yet... what if Illiaster is <i>Willpower</i>? Mortals in Hell get access to extra options for spending Willpower, and can recover it more often through their Vice; Demons can only recover it by consuming Illiaster, and Fallen Angels... well, they're a special case, aren't they?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T17:17:56-07:00","id":480941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/468141-converting-moongose-s-infernum-to-nwod?p=480222#post480222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Infernum didn\u00b4t have, sadly, rules for pacting with mortals or granting boons for souls. It was also implied demons, in recent times, didn\u00b4t deal directly with the mortal realm as much as before.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well I was rereading the book, but didn't finish, but I think it's more that most traffic with earth is humans in hell, then demons making it to earth, but that's appropriate to world of darkness anyway- there aren't infernal american pride parades down main street. <br /> <br /> A fun bit I got to is the timey whimey nature of hell- the present for hell corresponds from the 1600s to 2100s- so you could have an infernum dark era/bleeding edge game, which is interesting.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Amechra, okay, illiaster is just willpower, I could see it, it very much fills the niche of willpower for mortals. So is willpower just a quantifiable energy in hell that can be harvested through torture, making earth not a pleasant place for demons, or do demons just know how to harvest willpower through torture period, in which case a demon is just as powerful on earth as they are anywhere else? <br /> <br /> I would allow demons to have, normal virtues and vices (although inverted I'd think), a splat that can't recover willpower without torture farms that may or may not work on earth is a serious serious weakness, after all. It's not like normal vice and virtue gains would keep a willpower extensive splat in willpower. It could work like the generic monster rules from hunter, where vampires have extra willpower storage for their powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T19:13:31-07:00","id":481028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/468141-converting-moongose-s-infernum-to-nwod?p=480224#post480224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since you guys haven't decided on any hard mechanics yet... what if Illiaster is <i>Willpower</i>? Mortals in Hell get access to extra options for spending Willpower, and can recover it more often through their Vice; Demons can only recover it by consuming Illiaster, and Fallen Angels... well, they're a special case, aren't they?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That...actually makes a lot of sense. Iliaster could be Willpower after it's been sufficiently broken down to be released as a semi-spiritual substance.<br /> <br /> I would say demons have their own Willpower, but that makes incredible sense to have literal force of will stolen from others holding them together.<br /> <br /> Though, the pacting is where the Inferno rules come from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T21:06:59-07:00","id":481096,"title":"","content":"I think extracting Illiaster should be a thing Hell lets you do. It's just a law of the local physics that torture produces Illiaster, much like how Corruption is so prevalent there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T03:58:29-07:00","id":481257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/468141-converting-moongose-s-infernum-to-nwod?p=481096#post481096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think extracting Illiaster should be a thing Hell lets you do. It's just a law of the local physics that torture produces Illiaster, much like how Corruption is so prevalent there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I have absolutely no problem with that, but if one wants an infernum to run around the material world, are we picturing that like being a splicer in Bioshock, hoarding their liquid resources, are we picturing the houses having energy pipelines to demons on earth?<br /> <br /> Anyone given any thought on the demonic influence on other supernaturals?<br /> <br /> For example, are belial's brood just demons who are faustian sorcerers who harness corruption to grow mutations?<br /> <br /> Are the lucifuge people with a genetic talent for faustian sorcery thanks to genetic heritage, while the Enfants are humans who inherited specific demonic bloodlines? Or perhaps the Lucifuge are descendents of fallen angels and demonic nobles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T04:43:14-07:00","id":481265,"title":"","content":"Huh, I have the Infernum trilogy sitting on my bookshelves from back when I worked at Mongoose. Might crack them open and give them another look.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T04:47:53-07:00","id":481268,"title":"","content":"You know, thinking about this reminded me of the fact that originally Wraith was going to be about damned souls in hell,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T05:31:01-07:00","id":481279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/468141-converting-moongose-s-infernum-to-nwod?p=481268#post481268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You know, thinking about this reminded me of the fact that originally Wraith was going to be about damned souls in hell,</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Really?<br /> <br /> I did not know that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T07:34:21-07:00","id":481300,"title":"","content":"My understanding was that it was supposed to be how one dealt with the situation- either trying to escape, or accept your situation and become less human and more and more demonic as you assimilate.<br /> <br /> But the project seemed to be cursed, while playtesting it a pizza delivery guy hit something that caused a power outage in the house, something happened to the computer with the draft causing it to be lost, etc, they eventually decided it was too much hassle and made Wraith instead. <br /> <br /> Just as well I suppose, I don't think they'd have done demon the fallen after making that game, but I do admit it makes me curious. <br /> <br /> Does everyone remember the organization rules from Bleeding Edge? So I was thinking that the houses and other demonic organizations might be written up that way- having their own stats, vice and virtue, etc. <br /> <br /> So I was thinking that perhaps a member of that house of war might be able to regain willpower as if they had the vice of wrath, even if they don't personally have it, to represent that they're acting in accordance to their loyalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T16:17:01-07:00","id":481708,"title":"","content":"An idea for Demons:<br /> <br /> They get two Vices, neither of which are inverted. However, they may recover Willpower from their Vices twice per scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T20:07:18-07:00","id":481883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/468141-converting-moongose-s-infernum-to-nwod?p=481708#post481708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An idea for Demons:<br /> <br /> They get two Vices, neither of which are inverted. However, they may recover Willpower from their Vices twice per scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's along the lines of what I was thinking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T01:56:58-07:00","id":482124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/468141-converting-moongose-s-infernum-to-nwod?p=481883#post481883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's along the lines of what I was thinking.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And why were you thinking that?<br /> <br /> Is the idea of a patient demon waiting hundreds of years to see their plan come to fruition wrong somehow?<br /> <br /> Is the idea of a demon avoiding instant gratification for a better reward anethema?<br /> <br /> How about a demon having the diligence to not rest until their goal is met? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T06:08:14-07:00","id":482262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/468141-converting-moongose-s-infernum-to-nwod?p=482124#post482124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And why were you thinking that?<br /> <br /> Is the idea of a patient demon waiting hundreds of years to see their plan come to fruition wrong somehow?<br /> <br /> Is the idea of a demon avoiding instant gratification for a better reward anethema?<br /> <br /> How about a demon having the diligence to not rest until their goal is met?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I meant having the Vices and the Virtue, sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T07:56:13-07:00","id":482331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/468141-converting-moongose-s-infernum-to-nwod?p=482124#post482124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And why were you thinking that?<br /> <br /> Is the idea of a patient demon waiting hundreds of years to see their plan come to fruition wrong somehow?<br /> <br /> Is the idea of a demon avoiding instant gratification for a better reward anethema?<br /> <br /> How about a demon having the diligence to not rest until their goal is met?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking you could have them work like Angel Vices/Virtues - namely, they don't necessarily have to make sense as far as Human Vice/Virtue is concerned. Part of the suggestion is me being worried about the ability to simply refill their Fuel Stat instantly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T16:54:07-07:00","id":482951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/468141-converting-moongose-s-infernum-to-nwod?p=482331#post482331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking you could have them work like Angel Vices/Virtues - namely, they don't necessarily have to make sense as far as Human Vice/Virtue is concerned. Part of the suggestion is me being worried about the ability to simply refill their Fuel Stat instantly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Point. I do think the Houses need human Vices to focus on though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T19:49:39-07:00","id":483096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/468141-converting-moongose-s-infernum-to-nwod?p=482951#post482951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Point. I do think the Houses need human Vices to focus on though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good to me! Actually, that gives me an idea about the basic benefits of the Demon template:<br /> <br /> \u2022 You get two Vices. Demons who are members of a House gain that House's Vice as a third Vice.<br /> \u2022 Demons downgrade all damage from Fire to Bashing.<br /> \u2022 Corruption instead of Integrity.<br /> \u2022 Mutations.<br /> \u2022 Power Stat (What name?)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T22:00:31-07:00","id":483167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/468141-converting-moongose-s-infernum-to-nwod?p=482951#post482951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Point. I do think the Houses need human Vices to focus on though.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh okay, yeah, I wouldn't mind demons having the potential for weird vices (it's not like their culture is all that similar to ours, kindness seems like a valid vice in their culture for example) but the house vices do seem pretty human in nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T20:12:41-07:00","id":485031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/468141-converting-moongose-s-infernum-to-nwod?p=483096#post483096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds good to me! Actually, that gives me an idea about the basic benefits of the Demon template:<br /> <br /> \u2022 You get two Vices. Demons who are members of a House gain that House's Vice as a third Vice.<br /> \u2022 Demons downgrade all damage from Fire to Bashing.<br /> \u2022 Corruption instead of Integrity.<br /> \u2022 Mutations.<br /> \u2022 Power Stat (What name?)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seems like it.<br /> <br /> I'll also go with the Power Stat being Furnace-it burns brighter and better as you get more of it, but it needs more iliaster. I'll probably put in a starvation and fasting system though (it's not just &quot;run out of iliaster and it's getting close to game over&quot; it's &quot;run out of iliaster and you start weakening, but you can also accept weakness now to save up iliaster for later&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T22:05:09-07:00","id":485094,"title":"","content":"Given how NWoD 2e ruleset works, and my own uncertainty about the &quot;Cast From Hitpoints&quot; nature of iliaster in the D20 game, I would say a Furnace power stat as you describe would be the way to go, Leliel.<br /> <br /> I don't know if this has been touched upon, but, I think that the D20 mechanic of Fatebinding and the NWoD mechanic of &quot;mortals can burn Willpower&quot; dovetail together pretty nicely. It certainly cuts down on the amount of mechanics free-working we need to do if that is so.<br /> <br /> Hmm... for the sake of acquiring iliaster in the mortal world, what if we take advantage of the Unnatural Appetite (or whatever it's called) merit? In essence, hellspawn have the ability to leech Willpower from mortals and other races to convert it into iliaster. With the right powers/merits, though, they can also directly feed on &quot;power juice&quot; - essence, vitae, mana, quintessence, pyros, etc - as they have adapted to enhance their ability to feed. This makes running a hellspawn in Mundus chronicle much more viable.<br /> <br /> Also, recall how I mentioned hellspawn have a place to belong as one of their personal themes? Perhaps it'd be helpful if I tried my hand at a little essay for that, see if I can make it into something that works for inclusion into the project?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T22:07:47-07:00","id":485098,"title":"","content":"All good plans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T05:13:43-07:00","id":485342,"title":"","content":"Should faustian sorcerers get a specific merit, ritual or artifact to gather the iIiaster? I imagine demons would be delighted in teaching/granting their mortal associated means to collect the sweet nectar in exchange of a modicum tithe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T07:44:55-07:00","id":485404,"title":"","content":"Sorcerers have at least one spell to collect illaster, beyond that they could buy it.<br /> <br /> But anyway, Amechra, why on god's green earth would demon's need three vices? Giving them one naturally, and a second one through their house or other affiliation, fine. But the point of illaster is that demons need to eat it, making demons willpower regaining machines doesn't make any sense in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T13:50:55-07:00","id":485681,"title":"","content":"Well, I was also thinking that they'd be <i>leaky</i>. They'd have to pay Willpower to avoid starving, and they don't have a refill.<br /> <br /> I might have gone overboard though; one Vice and then one House Vice should be enough. Thanks.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T12:19:01-07:00","id":583729,"title":"","content":"So... what happened to this project? Is the original poster still around? I was hoping to see this take off, I really like this idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T13:02:44-07:00","id":583784,"title":"","content":"He is, it's just that he is involved in other things, too.<br /> <br /> Thanks for reminding me this exists, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T02:42:01-07:00","id":604560,"title":"","content":"Just some general thoughts on Hellspawn/other splat opinions/attitudes.<br /> <br /> Vampires: Both species have a similar nature, in that they must prey upon the very essence of mortals to survive from night to night; vampires on the essence of life, hellspawn on the essence of the soul. This similarity breeds amusement in hellspawn and unease in vampires. Those rare members of the Kindred who have dared to cross the divide and enter the Pit have found that, whilst they are hardpressed to find human prey, they can feed upon the gory fluids of the River Styx for nourishment, much as they can in the Underworld, and that the alien light of the Morningstar is no threat to their unlives. Thusly, there is a small, but well-entrenched and slowly growing population of Kindred who have forsaken the struggles of the nightly hunt to instead carve a place for themselves amongst their fellow monsters.<br /> <br /> Werewolves: For the most part, hellspawn and werewolves have little interest in each other. However, a lodge exists known as the Benandanti, who use lodge rituals to enter the Pit and try to make off with the damned souls there. Though their philosophy is that this is necessary for the health of the Shadow, most of the lodge's members are undergoing a corruption of their own, similar to that suffered by vampires who feast upon the spectral blood of the Underworld or through ectophagia, making it harder for them to regain Essence from any source other than devouring the damned.<br /> <br /> Mages: The Awakened and the Hellspawn rarely interact with each other. Mages have far too much power of their own to make Faustian bargains, and though the sheer potency of an Awakened soul tempts many a hellspawn, that same power and the fearsome prowess of their own faustians makes them wary.<br /> <br /> Prometheans: There is a strange kinship between hellspawn and prometheans. Both are unnatural abominations, divine energies shackled into primitive shells of meat and bone. Though hellspawn find the Pilgrimage incomprehensible, they offer prometheans a very rare perspective on who and what they are, and what they can become. Though it cannot avoid mentioning that, between the hellspawn's immunity to Disquiet and the Pit's immunity to the Wasteland, there is a tiny number of prometheans who have forsaken the idea of being human to instead make a place for themselves amongst monsters.<br /> <br /> Changelings: Needless to say, changelings avoid hellspawn like the plague, and so hellspawn rarely get involved with them. There are similarities there - the binding nature of one's word - but not enough to account for paranoia on one side and disinterest on the other.<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters: Those who hunt ghosts have to wrestle with the temptation that, if all else fails, hellspawn offer a truly drastic final solution. A ghost hauled screaming off to hell to be devoured certainly will never plague the living again, after all. Still, the idea sits uneasily with the vast majority of sin-eaters.<br /> <br /> Mummies: Fixated on the whims of the Judges, the Risen have little cause to interact with hellspawn, who likewise find little reason to interact with mummies.<br /> <br /> Demons (Unchained): Neither breed knows quite what to make of the other. One is a creature of eldritch programming and alien geometries, the other a creature of profane magic and corrupt flesh. Still, they share a common bond, of the slave that rebelled to find its own place, and so those rare occasions where they cross paths they can find common ground. Some of the Unchained wonder if the Pit is where they belong, if it could be the Hell that they seek so ardently.<br /> <br /> Mortals: For the most part, humans are nothing but food to the hellspawn, and they treat them accordingly. With a world of their own to retreat to, most hellspawn are far bolder in their depredations than other creatures of the night, confident that they can retreat beyond humanity's reach should it lash out in blind and clumsy retribution.<br /> <br /> Hunters: Food that dares to bite back would be the succinct summary of the typical hellspawn attitude towards hunters. Many hellspawn particularly enjoy defeating (or eating) hunters, in order to forcibly remind humanity of its place as livestock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T13:33:29-07:00","id":729780,"title":"","content":"In addition to bumping this project, I was curious; what would people be more interested in playing, if this took off? Games in the Infernum, or the &quot;weird world&quot; standard of NWoD, playing a Hellspawn on Earth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T18:42:08-07:00","id":730682,"title":"","content":"Well unless things are changed, existing in the material world of nwod would be...punishing, and that the vast majority of splats could find themselves in the Pit just like mortals, I think focusing on games in the Pit would make sense.<br /> <br /> Hmm, I wonder what demons would think of beasts- creatures who feed on fear, as opposed to pain, capable of traveling back and forth as they please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 10-26-2015, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T21:34:21-07:00","id":733895,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\">Welcome to Scenic Hell!</span><br /> While you are here, there are some things you should keep in mind:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Those of you who are Mortal are in luck! You have a few more options for what to do with your Willpower!<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">\u2022 You can spend it to give someone else a -2 penalty on their roll - even if you aren't the one that roll is directed towards! Hell rewards spite, you see.<br /> \u2022 You can spend Willpower to do some creative editing of the universe - by the local rules, wishes <i>do</i> come true! Once per story, you can spend one Willpower to have something good happen. It will take shape over the course of the next few Scenes, will cost you some stuff that you didn't want to spend, and will have some glaring flaws in implementation, but it <i>will</i> ultimately be good for you. You can spend additional Willpower to remove some of these drawbacks on a one-for-one basis, to a maximum of two points of Willpower.</div> \u2022 Speaking of Willpower, it's tangible here. We call it Iliaster. Anyone can spend one Willpower to have one Iliaster appear, taking the form of a thin plasmic fluid. You might want a cup to collect it. You can also get it out of people through torture. Again, the local rules say that Success on a roll made to torture someone drains them of one Willpower and produces that much Iliaster. Again, you might want a cup to collect the stuff.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T01:25:35-07:00","id":888949,"title":"","content":"I wonder whatever happened to Leliel. But then, I couldn't get my own, far simpler &quot;Resident Evil&quot; fansplat off the ground, so I guess it's no surprise that this didn't work out. A pity; Infernum is one of the true gems of D20's myriad 3rd party spinoffs, so a Chronicles of Darkness spinoff would be a great thing, I feel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T07:04:57-07:00","id":889079,"title":"","content":"I lost interest when I realized how large a project this would be, and I was dividing my time among other things.<br /> <br /> Sorry. I'm just suited to making antagonists and lesser templates, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}